WEBVTT

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:30.000
WELL, HERE WE GO.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.840
Let's go again.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.900
You ready?

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.630
Let's get right on it today.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.010
So I'm gonna start off with a little bit

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.830
of alizarin crimson.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.030
Canvas has already been covered

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.130
with a thin, even coat of Magic White.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.170
So let's just put a tiny little bit of crimson

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.010
right up here.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.140
I thought today we'd do a,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.030
maybe we'll do a little water wheel.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:49.990
A lot in this painting,

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.910
so I'm gonna just take off and get started here.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:54.830
Without cleaning the brush,

00:00:54.830 --> 00:01:00.000
go right into a little tiny bit of phthalo blue.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:05.690
the edges and bring it right up to the crimson.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:11.400
Just like so.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.180
Okay, just want a little spot in the center there

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.000
that's got a little life in it.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.400
Now with a clean, dry brush,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.460
just very gently blend all this together.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.080
Most of this pinkish color will just disappear.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.900
I just want a little light spot up here.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.510
I think we're ready.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.450
Okay, now I'm gonna go right into

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.920
Alizarin Crimson and Prussian Blue.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.260
Just mix it on the brush.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.020
Maybe we'll put some little distant tree indications

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.780
way back here in the distance.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.710
Just drop 'em in.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.090
We're not looking for a lot of detail.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.570
We want these to be far, far away.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:56.460
Just, just little things happening in the distance.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.620
Oh, there's one.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.370
just wherever you think they might be.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.930
Now, let's go right into some Van Dyke Brown,

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.700
a little alizarin crimson,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.980
and just begin dropping in a few shapes.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.480
We'll put some sap green in there, too.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.760
So we've got sap green, alizarin crimson,

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.390
Van Dyke Brown.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.100
There's a little tree,

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.370
just wherever you think there might be one.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.330
Let's just drop some little things in.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.570
And don't kill all these little things

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.920
that you put back here to indicate trees

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.120
that are far, far away.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.000
Leave them in there.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:39.280
Maybe there's a big tree here, something like so.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:45.820
And we'll give him some little friends down here.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:50.850
Okay, that gives us a quick little background.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.950
Really want to spend some time working on the water wheel,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.180
so we'll try to just do this real rapidly

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.460
and get into the serious stuff.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:08.130
Okay, now let's take, let's use the fan brush today.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.290
We'll just take some Van Dyke Brown,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.350
put a little bit of white on one side,

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.880
brown and white.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.440
We'll just jump right up here

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.280
and put a quick little trunk right in that.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.990
Maybe just one over here.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.050
A few little sticks and twigs.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.000
Wash the fan brush.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.900
Okay, now let's use the one inch brush

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.640
and put some highlights on these.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.290
Let's put a little bit of magic white into the brush

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.930
just to thin it down a little.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.140
Yellow and sap green.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.280
Yellow and sap green.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.020
Makes a beautiful, beautiful tree color.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.420
There we go.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.260
And just drop some little highlights here.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.160
Let's get a little bit of yellow ochre in here, too.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:02.960
What the heck?

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.570
Let's put a few little highlights back in that little tree.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.490
A few little things happening all over.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:20.260
Okay.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.940
And we'll put some sap green and yellow on this one.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.980
Maybe we'll brighten that up a touch.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.000
There we go.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:35.170
That's better.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.690
Paint on the brush and we can lay some right in there.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:43.210
Just let these little leaves just flow right off your brush.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.770
They live right in this little one inch brush.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:50.580
You have to sort of scare them out sometime.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.920
Little bit of Indian yellow, too.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.850
I like Indian yellow, it's a very transparent color.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.320
Very nice if you're ever working on the black canvases.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.200
And we'll drop a few little things in there,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.410
a little permanent red.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.940
Put a little red bush right there.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:16.860
What the heck?

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.420
Okay, now maybe somewhere right along in here

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.480
we have to make a decision.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.850
Maybe there's a little stream coming right down through here.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.910
Let's add a tiny bit of blue to that.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.000
Maybe just one.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.020
right down here like so.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:39.890
Put the dark in first, and a little bit of Van Dyke Brown,

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:45.590
and we can put some banks back here.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.970
Just however you want the land to flow.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:52.030
There we go.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.790
And we can take some brown and white,

00:05:53.790 --> 00:06:00.000
a little touch of blue, make some nice highlight colors.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.940
and just drop right on there.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.380
This is just sort of a gray color.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.670
Something like so.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.840
Now then, let's take the fan brush.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.880
We'll use some yellow ochre, sap green.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.200
Let's just put some little grassy things

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.780
that grow right down the bank back here.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.750
They are.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.220
Now let's let them go.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.000
Wherever you think they should be.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.370
put some right over in here.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.450
Follow the lay of the land, so it gives the impression

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.810
that the land's coming down like that.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:45.030
Okay, now, a little magic white, a little firm white,

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.260
and we can slip right up in here

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.340
and begin adding a little water.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.940
Make it look like a happy little stream.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:57.070
It's just playing through the meadow.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.000
Maybe there's a little, bloop, right there.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:11.900
and drop them in, just so it's not completely even.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.820
There we go, that gives us a bubbling

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.490
little stream coming down.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:20.960
Gotta have something to turn the wheel.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.750
Then let's go right back in here.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:30.000
A bit of the dark color, it's just Van Dyke brown.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.810
to give us a nice base.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:46.790
A bit of the highlight, and then we can put

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:52.390
some little grassy areas back in there.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:56.400
Still following the lay of the land.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.680
Always try to follow the lay of the land.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:07.900
Add a little bit of sap green there.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:13.200
It's about time we made a decision here.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.200
Where is our water wheel gonna be?

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.900
And like we did when we did the covered bridge,

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.360
it's really better to scrape out a basic shape.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.600
Just decide basically where your wheel is gonna be.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.050
And it removes the loose, thin paint,

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:28.460
and it gives you a guide to follow.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.000
And sometimes that's very helpful

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.100
We'll just, ooh, isn't that terrible going through there

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.760
and scraping off all those trees you worked so hard to put on?

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:41.790
We need a tall building for this wheel to be on.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.650
Tall building.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.370
So how about there?

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.140
Be brave.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.050
Just drop it down.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:54.530
It really makes it easier, once again,

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.140
if you get this loose paint off the canvas.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.000
It really, really and truly helps.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.340
Okay, now we can just take the Van Dyke brown,

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:10.990
just go right up here, and begin building us a house.

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:12.490
And all we're doing is putting the brown in,

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.780
so we don't have to worry about detail or shape right now.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.170
Just drop it in.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:25.600
We'll come back and begin adding all the little highlights.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.810
here, a little back heave on that building.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:41.590
And we need some long boards, just drop 'em in.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.480
Let 'em fall right off the knife.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:51.890
There we go, a tall building here so our wheel,

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:54.540
we want a big wheel, big wheel.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.040
I think my son used to ride one of those

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.270
and he was very small.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:10.530
That gives us a basic shape for our building.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:15.500
We can begin putting in some highlights.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.190
Let's use a little bit of the umber Van Dyke.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:23.690
Touch of titanium white.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:24.830
Maybe a little more of the umber.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.920
Want it a little more into the reddish hue.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.840
There we go, that's a nice color.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.820
and makes your paint marbly so that all kinds of colors

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.960
happen when you come down here.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.900
Old building, I like old buildings.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.780
They're so much more fun to paint than bright shiny new ones.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:53.510
Little more there, just brighten that rascal up a little bit.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:59.350
Need some right down this side over here, now.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.860
Let's add a little bit more of the Van Dyke brown,

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.750
darken this color up a little bit,

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.720
and we'll do the dark side of the building first.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.760
Touch, and just go down.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:16.330
Let the paint break so it looks like old wood here.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:20.190
Touch, and go down.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:27.040
Isn't that something?

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.060
Okay, now, the front of the

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:33.870
mill here, we need to have a little bit lighter

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:36.950
because the light's gonna be striking in this direction.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:38.370
So I've just added a little bit of white

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:46.170
to the same color, and just drop it right down like that.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:51.540
It's nice looking old wood.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.880
Take a little bit of color on the knife, a dark color,

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.800
and we can put some boards in here.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:04.980
like so.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:06.280
A lot of times when they built these,

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:09.790
they'd put a little, maybe there's right up here,

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:14.560
just a little tiny little projection right there.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:18.260
Just drop that right in.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.400
Fill that up full of dark paint.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:25.770
Then we can come back and highlight it.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.810
Just put a highlight right there.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:36.150
There, this one right here, quite bright.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:40.650
Just come across.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:47.310
Straight down, cut that off.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.440
Get you the right angle in there.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:52.960
You can put some little board indications.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.030
We got a little roof.

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.300
That's all there is to it.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.700
Okay, you ready to build the wheel?

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:02.490
Probably the same thing as before.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:03.970
It's easier if you sort of scrape off

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.740
some of this loose paint.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:09.790
So let's start right here and make part of the wheel.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:13.930
And then right here, ooh, there goes the building.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.630
Now one of the big things here,

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.250
I want this to show through.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.840
It's very important to me that this part show through

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.970
so you can see depth inside of this wheel.

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:27.150
So we just scrape that right off like that.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:30.000
Go right into the Van Dyke Brown, touch.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:33.900
and sort of fill it up.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:42.750
Touch, come around, just come right on around.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:48.490
How do you make a round circle with a square knife?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:53.580
That's your challenge for the day.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:56.510
You'll see the back of the wheel back here,

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:57.780
so we'll just do that.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:03.770
Now let's just take a little bit of paint thinner,

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:06.660
a little bit of yellow ochre,

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.010
and let's just highlight this little rascal here

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:17.470
a little bit, just to highlight it.

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:21.660
And we can work that paint right in.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:27.700
Maybe we'll take the fan brush, it's a little faster.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.000
There, that's better.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:38.020
Now, we need a little bit of water on this wheel.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:42.000
So let's start right up in here somewhere.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.100
Maybe there's just the littlest indication of water

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:51.220
and as it comes down, more and more and more.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:53.490
Now, you could go real slow and put the water

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.250
in between each one of these little pegs,

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.490
but this is much easier.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:15:00.000
Then we go back and put the pegs over the water, sneaky.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:09.350
We just drop that right in, come right on up like that.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:12.430
Back to our little fan brush.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:21.470
Bring this right just like that.

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:26.820
So we got a basic water wheel already, okay.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:32.070
Got to have something to hold the wheel up,

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.040
so let's just do this.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.960
Come all the way through that way,

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.910
all the way through that way.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:43.790
Maybe all the way through that way, and that way.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.050
Just have all kind of fun.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:49.060
We need a rod that goes through here,

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:53.510
a big shaft to hold it up, so we'll put that in.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:59.060
Now, let's put some spokes on the other side there.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.800
Let's bring this one right on down like that.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:11.660
Right over here, there, and maybe there.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:15.620
Now on these, we need a little bit of highlight

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.700
on the ones on the outside, so just touch.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.100
Just put a little bit of highlight out here.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:23.730
Don't overdo, just enough to make 'em stand out.

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:26.350
Create a little depth in there.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:30.000
We can take our liner brush and see

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:35.810
to smooth all this up.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:40.290
By golly, we got a pretty good wheel going here.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.690
And at home, you have a lot of time,

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:44.640
so you can really put some detail into this if you'd like.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:48.530
Here, we're just trying to show you how to do it.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:51.570
Okay, got us a wheel.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.820
Maybe there's another little projection

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:58.930
that comes right out through here, just like this.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:05.040
That easy, just drop it in.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:11.640
Okay, we'll put a little bit of highlight on that.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:20.000
Need some boards to hold that little sheet up out here.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:38.150
A little bit of highlight out here, brighten it there.

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:41.690
That's what we're looking for.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:46.210
Dark area right there, there's always a little shadow there.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.060
A little tiny shadow in this one too.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.890
There we go.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:57.650
Okay, now let's go right over here

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.320
and decide where the land is.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:03.740
Here, maybe it comes down like so,

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:07.330
so it just leaves you a little stream back here.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:13.190
Just drop it in.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:19.330
Fan brush, a little bit of the sap green and yellow.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:26.610
Passy area's coming right down here.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.460
Isn't that something?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.920
Now we gotta have something to hold this wheel up,

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.900
we don't want it just to float out there in space.

